ansfer Protocol) client requests a custom small block size and receives a standard response, it falls back to the default block size without resizing the allocated memory buffer. A malicious TFTP server can exploit this issue by sending standard-sized network packets during a transfer, causing a heap buffer overflow. This flaw allows an attacker to achieve arbitrary code execution or cause a Denial of Service (DoS) by crashing the application.","type":"unreviewed","severity":"high","repository_advisory_url":null,"source_code_location":"","identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-r558-xpjx-65pf","type":"GHSA"},{"value":"CVE-2026-124737","type":"CVE"}],"references":["https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-124737","https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-124737","https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2571607","https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-r558-xpjx-65pf"],"published_at":"2026-11-11T12:31:40Z","updated_at":"2026-11-11T12:31:48Z","github_reviewed_at":null,"nvd_published_at":"2026-11-11T10:16:43Z","withdrawn_at":null,"vulnerabilities":[],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","score":7.5},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":null,"score":0.0}},"cwes":[{"cwe_id":"CWE-787","name":"Out-of-bounds Write"}],"credits":[],"comments":0,"cvss":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","score":7.5},"epss":{"percentage":0.00454,"percentile":0.39885}},{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-38v2-q8r5-xfrm","cve_id":"CVE-2026-103883","url":"https://api.github.com/advisories/GHSA-38v2-q8r5-xfrm","html_url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-38v2-q8r5-xfrm","summary":"The 6Storage Rentals plugin for WordPress is vulnerable to Authentication Bypass leading to...","description":"The 6Storage Rentals plugin for WordPress is vulnerable to Authentication Bypass leading to Administrator Account Takeover in all versions up to, and including, 2.31.0. The vulnerability exists because the `six_storage_portal_registration()` AJAX handler — registered on `wp_ajax_six_storage_portal_plugin_registration` — performs no capability check and no nonce verification before writing the caller-supplied `six_storage_online_api_url` POST parameter to the site-wide option of the same name; the unauthenticated `six_storage_create_wp_user()` handler then redeems a transient seeded from that attacker-controlled URL's response and unconditionally calls `wp_set_current_user()` and `wp_set_auth_cookie()` with no ownership or credential verification. This makes it possible for authenticated attackers, with Subscriber-level access and above, to authenticate as any existing WordPress user — including any administrator whose email address is known or guessable — resulting in full site compromise. This issue represents an incomplete fix for a prior vulnerability: the 2.29.0 remediation moved the target email out of POST data into a server-side transient, but because any Subscriber can still overwrite the outbound API URL that populates that transient, the full authentication bypass chain remains exploitable in three AJAX requests.","type":"unreviewed","severity":"high","repository_advisory_url":null,"source_code_location":"","identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-38v2-q8r5-xfrm","type":"GHSA"},{"value":"CVE-2026-103883","type":"CVE"}],"references":["https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-103883","https://plugins.trac.wordpress.org/browser/6storage-rentals/tags/2.31.0/inc/Base/Six_Storage_DashboardController.php#L14","https://plugins.trac.wordpress.org/browser/6storage-rentals/tags/2.31.0/inc/Base/Six_Storage_DashboardController.php#L4126","https://plugins.trac.wordpress.org/browser/6storage-rentals/tags/2.31.0/inc/Base/Six_Storage_SignInControllerSixStorage.php#L90","https://plugins.trac.wordpress.org/browser/6storage-rentals/tags/2.31.0/inc/Pages/Admin/Six_Storage_WpAdmin.php#L39","https://plugins.trac.wordpress.org/browser/6storage-rentals/tags/2.31.0/inc/Pages/Admin/Six_Storage_WpAdmin.php#L708","https://www.wordfence.com/threat-intel/vulnerabilities/id/67b82539-8582-4bb4-ad4c-b626233b6075?source=cve","https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-38v2-q8r5-xfrm"],"published_at":"2026-11-11T12:31:40Z","updated_at":"2026-11-11T12:31:48Z","github_reviewed_at":null,"nvd_published_at":"2026-11-11T12:18:14Z","withdrawn_at":null,"vulnerabilities":[],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","score":8.8},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":null,"score":0.0}},"cwes":[{"cwe_id":"CWE-287","name":"Improper Authentication"}],"credits":[],"comments":0,"cvss":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","score":8.8},"epss":{"percentage":0.00708,"percentile":0.53939}},{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-hh26-8w49-8vg3","cve_id":"CVE-2026-111792","url":"https://api.github.com/advisories/GHSA-hh26-8w49-8vg3","html_url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-hh26-8w49-8vg3","summary":"Uncontrolled Recursion vulnerability in Apache XML Graphics Batik.\n\n\n\nThis issue affects Apache...","description":"Uncontrolled Recursion vulnerability in Apache XML Graphics Batik.\n\n\n\nThis issue affects Apache XML Graphics Batik: through 1.19.\n\n\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 1.20, which fixes the issue.","type":"unreviewed","severity":"unknown","repository_advisory_url":null,"source_code_location":"","identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-hh26-8w49-8vg3","type":"GHSA"},{"value":"CVE-2026-111792","type":"CVE"}],"references":["https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-111792","https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/BATIK-1397","https://lists.apache.org/thread.html/dn70ltz1o9sg88dd87wcyh4v73fk2tnm","http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/11/11/14","https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-hh26-8w49-8vg3"],"published_at":"2026-11-11T12:31:40Z","updated_at":"2026-11-11T21:33:59Z","github_reviewed_at":null,"nvd_published_at":"2026-11-11T11:17:11Z","withdrawn_at":null,"vulnerabilities":[],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":null,"score":0.0},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":null,"score